1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:02,958
On Treatment

2
00:00:03,916 --> 00:00:10,625
After consultation, plan approval, and completion 
of planning steps, your treatment begins. 

3
00:00:11,125 --> 00:00:17,333
You will return to the department for treatment during 
your personalized treatment plan’s dates and times.

4
00:00:17,541 --> 00:00:21,250
 Frequency and number of treatments varies 
from patient to patient. 

5
00:00:21,541 --> 00:00:27,083
You may come back daily, every other day, 
or be done with treatment all together.

6
00:00:29,416 --> 00:00:34,750
How long each treatment session takes can 
vary depending on your particular situation, 

7
00:00:34,750 --> 00:00:42,875
but on average they last around 20 minutes and 
entail two steps: set-up and delivery of radiation.

8
00:00:43,291 --> 00:00:48,375
For set-up, you will be placed in the same 
position as your CT simulation scan 

9
00:00:48,583 --> 00:00:53,583
and a cone-beam CT will be performed to 
ensure proper placement. 

10
00:00:54,291 --> 00:00:58,750
 After being placed in the correct position 
and the position is verified,

11
00:00:59,083 --> 00:01:02,083
 external beam radiation to the target area begins. 

12
00:01:06,166 --> 00:01:07,166
Once a week,

13
00:01:07,166 --> 00:01:10,916
while you are receiving treatment,
you will see your doctor in the clinic

14
00:01:10,916 --> 00:01:16,250
who will check in with you
during this on treatment visit or OTV.

15
00:01:16,458 --> 00:01:20,708
This is a great time to discuss
any side effects or other symptoms

16
00:01:20,708 --> 00:01:24,583
you may be feeling, and dive
into what treatments are available.

17
00:01:24,583 --> 00:01:28,083
Additionally,
you may meet with our registered dietitian

18
00:01:28,083 --> 00:01:31,083
to discuss your weight
and nutritional status.

19
00:01:31,416 --> 00:01:34,625
There are also many other support staff
available to you.

20
00:01:34,916 --> 00:01:38,375
Should you require their services,
such as our social worker

21
00:01:38,458 --> 00:01:41,458
and many skilled registered nurses.

22
00:01:41,791 --> 00:01:45,333
While we are scheduled to see you
once a week at minimum.

23
00:01:45,333 --> 00:01:49,166
If you have any of the following
or any urgent concerns

24
00:01:49,166 --> 00:01:54,125
in between OTVs
please do not hesitate to contact us.

25
00:01:54,333 --> 00:01:55,166
A temperature of

26
00:01:55,166 --> 00:02:00,416
104°F 38°C or higher.

27
00:02:00,541 --> 00:02:02,125
Chills.

28
00:02:02,125 --> 00:02:05,125
Increasing pain or discomfort.

29
00:02:05,125 --> 00:02:07,500
Increased redness or swelling

30
00:02:07,500 --> 00:02:10,541
or skin that is hard or hot to the touch.

31
00:02:11,166 --> 00:02:15,041
A rash or blistering of your skin
in the treated area.

32
00:02:15,416 --> 00:02:18,416
Drainage
from your skin in the treated area.

33
00:02:19,250 --> 00:02:22,625
Any new open areas
or changes to your skin.
